it's minus 15 degrees celsius  and herman has been on his feet since 6  a.m  he's one of dozens of people waiting to  give parcels to the inmates of the  sacharova detention center  hermann is here for his flatmates  fidlanatsvitkova  she was sentenced to five days for  participating in anti-government  protests in moscow  we've collected warm clothes here's a  sweater  and a blanket  tears those are my friends in there  over 7 000 people have been arrested  since the protests began  the police have been especially brutal  in moscow and saint petersburg  they've even taken people away who had  nothing to do with the protests  just because they happened to be in the  area  this group of young people had to sit in  a freezing police van for seven  hours they were told there wasn't enough  space in the jails for them  these images show conditions in the  sacha rova detention center near moscow  overcrowded cells inmates having to  share the bare metal beds  there's an open latrine right there in  the room  herman's flatmate svetlana tsvetkova  also had to endure these conditions  after five days svetlana is released  she's relieved to be back at home with  herman in their kitchen  she says she wasn't able to contact the  outside world during her incarceration  and was overjoyed to receive hermann's  parcel  she shows us a video from when she was  arrested  she and other protesters were standing  in front of the jail where opposition  activist alexei navalny was being  detained  the police surrounded them and arrested  them one by one  [Music]  someone i'm close to whom i care for  was kidnapped even if they arrested a  legal basis  it was totally unacceptable from a  humanitarian viewpoint  we're law-abiding citizens we respect  our constitution  we're not doing anything that's  prohibited and suddenly this happens  on top of that we're told it's right no  it's wrong  it's simply awful svetlana tells us she  didn't get  anything to eat for the first three days  after her arrest  because she was taken from one police  station to the next and nobody felt  responsible  she was so tense the whole time that  she's only just begun to realize how  inhumane the situation was  like many other protesters hermann and  svetlana did not take to the streets  only because navalny was arrested  they were demonstrating against the  current political system more generally  and then try to tell us how to behave  this system is wrong  many of the saharaova detainees have now  been released  and they think much the same way many  want to take to the streets again to  protest  against the system
 

